## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a robust, observable streaming pipeline with runtime policy-based validation and safe failure handling at scale.

## Key Concepts

- Streaming ingestion with Pub/Sub and Dataflow (Beam)
- Dynamic policy engine (Firestore) for field/type validation
- Dead-letter/quarantine in Cloud Storage with metadata
- Custom metrics in Cloud Monitoring for data quality
- Schema drift resilience and backpressure handling

## Code Example

```python
# Example: skeleton DoFn using Firestore policy to validate records
class ValidateWithPolicy(DoFn):
    def setup(self):
        self.firestore_client = firestore.Client()
        self.policy_cache = {}

    def process(self, element):
        # Load policy from Firestore with caching
        policy = self.get_policy(element.get('schema_version'))

        # Validate fields/types against policy
        if self.validate_record(element, policy):
            yield element
        else:
            # Send invalid records to dead-letter sink
            yield pvalue.TaggedOutput('invalid', {
                'record': element,
                'metadata': {
                    'timestamp': datetime.utcnow().isoformat(),
                    'validation_errors': self.get_validation_errors(element, policy)
                }
            })
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests end-to-end real-time data engineering competencies on GCP, including multi-tenant isolation, dynamic schema evolution, data contracts, and rollback semantics, plus cross-cloud replication and testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time ingestion with Pub/Sub and Dataflow templates
- Per-tenant isolation using partitioned BigQuery datasets
- Central schema registry in Data Catalog for dynamic evolution
- End-to-end lineage and data contracts
- 24-hour per-tenant rollback via BigQuery time travel
- Cross-region replication to Snowflake via Snowpipe

## Code Example

```java
// Dataflow pipeline with tenant isolation and schema validation
public class TenantPipeline {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        PipelineOptions options = PipelineOptionsFactory.fromArgs(args).create();
        Pipeline pipeline = Pipeline.create(options);

        pipeline
            .apply("Read from Pub/Sub", PubsubIO.readMessagesWithAttributes()
                .fromSubscription(options.getSubscription()))
            .apply("Extract tenant ID", ParDo.of(new ExtractTenantDoFn()))
            .apply("Validate against schema", ParDo.of(new SchemaValidationDoFn()))
            .apply("Write to tenant BigQuery", new TenantBigQueryWrite());

        pipeline.run();
    }
}
```
